<body>
    <h1>Fix NVIDIA Driver issue causing inability to boot</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>If your Ubuntu 22 system no longer boots due to NVIDIA driver is=
sues, you can use a recovery method to purge the NVIDIA drivers from the co=
mmand line. Here's a step-by-step guide:</p>
<h3 id=3D"FixNVIDIADriverissuecausinginabilitytoboot-1.BootintoRecoveryMode=
">1. <strong>Boot into Recovery Mode</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Reboot your system.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Hold <strong>Shift</strong> or press <strong>Esc</strong> during boot to=
 access the GRUB menu.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Select <strong>Advanced options for Ubuntu</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Choose a <strong>Recovery mode</strong> kernel.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"FixNVIDIADriverissuecausinginabilitytoboot-2.DroptoRootShell">2. =
<strong>Drop to Root Shell</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>In the recovery menu, choose <strong>Root</strong> to drop into a root s=
hell.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"FixNVIDIADriverissuecausinginabilitytoboot-3.RemountFileSystemwit=
hWritePermissions">3. <strong>Remount File System with Write Permissions</s=
trong></h3>
<p>By default, the file system is mounted as read-only. Remount it as read-=
write:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">bash</p=
re>
</div>
</div>
<p>Copy code</p>
<p><code>mount -o remount,rw /</code></p>
<h3 id=3D"FixNVIDIADriverissuecausinginabilitytoboot-4.PurgeNVIDIADrivers">=
4. <strong>Purge NVIDIA Drivers</strong></h3>
<p>Run the following commands to remove all NVIDIA-related packages:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">bash</p=
re>
</div>
</div>
<p>Copy code</p>
<p><code>apt-get purge '^nvidia-.*' -y apt-get autoremove --purge -y apt-ge=
t clean</code></p>
<h3 id=3D"FixNVIDIADriverissuecausinginabilitytoboot-5.ReinstallDefaultNouv=
eauDriver(Optional)">5. <strong>Reinstall Default Nouveau Driver (Optional)=
</strong></h3>
<p>If you want to fall back to the open-source Nouveau driver:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">bash</p=
re>
</div>
</div>
<p>Copy code</p>
<p><code>apt-get install xserver-xorg-video-nouveau -y</code></p>
<h3 id=3D"FixNVIDIADriverissuecausinginabilitytoboot-6.UpdateGRUB">6. <stro=
ng>Update GRUB</strong></h3>
<p>Update your GRUB configuration to ensure smooth booting:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">bash</p=
re>
</div>
</div>
<p>Copy code</p>
<p><code>update-grub</code></p>
<h3 id=3D"FixNVIDIADriverissuecausinginabilitytoboot-7.ReboottheSystem">7. =
<strong>Reboot the System</strong></h3>
<p>Exit the root shell and reboot:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">bash</p=
re>
</div>
</div>
<p>Copy code</p>
<p><code>reboot</code></p>
<p>Your system should now boot with the NVIDIA drivers removed. Let me know=
 if you encounter any issues during these steps.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
